Search fields: an input of type search keeps a cancel button (a 'searchcancel' part after its text, Chromium's
-webkit-search-cancel-button) sized by Chromium's rule (9px at a 13px font, scaled with the font size and rounded,
within 5px to 21px), centered across the content box at its end. The text neither enters nor paints under the
button's margin box (Element::SetClipAreaRightInset). The button hides while the field is empty; a click on it, or
Escape in a non-empty field, empties the field and dispatches 'search' (cleared); Enter dispatches 'search' after
its change.
